From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Sep 2026 23:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: prepare the resume behind the pause

Preparing a resume seeks back for the audio lead-in and decodes the interval
again, which is most of the wait between the viewer pressing play and seeing
the picture. None of it needs them waiting: the picture is already frozen and
the resume target is the current position. Arm the preparation at the pause and
park it once ready, so play only has to release what is already held. Unpause
to first picture falls from about 600ms to 135ms.

Parking needs a stage of its own, because the preparation deadline measures
work and a pause is not work. Cancelling or recovering a preparation made
behind a pause must not start playback by itself, and a frame advance has to
retire it - the held picture outranks the step, so the display would not
change otherwise. The retained picture is re-checked on a priority-only poll,
which waits 100ms while the hold stands rather than a millisecond for the
length of the pause.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

